# Fixing Thin Timetable Cards

## The Bug
The cards appeared vertically thin or "squashed" even after increasing the `minHeight` parameter earlier. This occurred because table row cells (`td`) were using a CSS trick `height: 1px` while setting `min-height: 140px` to attempt stretching. While this stretches the *cell* correctly, any `absolute`ly positioned child element (like the new timetable cards) asks its parent "What is your height?" so it can calculate `height: 100%`. The parent returns `1px`, causing the absolute card to crush vertically.

## Changes Made
- Removed the `height: 1px` trick on both Vertical and Horizontal layout cells.
- Statically assigned `height: 140` to the row styles. 
- Now, the absolute cards ask for `100%` height and correctly inherit `140px` instead of `1px`. 

## Validation
- The UI should now dynamically map 100% heights within the rows. The cards will be appropriately thick rectangles matching the `140px` bounds edge-to-edge.
